    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency score makes him our premier start. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable matchup against Seth Lugo, despite the slight efficiency drag from Lugo\u2019s elite hold on the basepaths. Supporting the top of the order, **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) and **Andy Pages** (71.40) represent elite value against shaky arms like Schultz and Bratt. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as a high-floor play (70.23); his score is bolstered significantly by a +14% platoon edge against Warren, proving the importance of isolating favorable handedness splits to maximize our 5x5 output.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Brayan Rocchio** on the bench. Despite a solid 56.28 score and a favorable matchup against Phillips, **Brayan Rocchio** ultimately failed to crack the starting rotation because the depth of our middle infield and outfield creates a higher efficiency threshold for entry. Similarly, **Miguel Vargas** remains on the bench despite an elite 0.403 xwOBA; his score of 56.21 was throttled by a tough catcher matchup and a marginal plate appearance projection compared to the consistent volume expected from starters like **Sam Antonacci**. \n\nWe are monitoring the stolen base potential closely today: **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill** are high-priority starts, not just for their solid projections, but because the slow delivery of their respective opposing pitchers creates an optimal environment for aggressive base running. While **Liam Hicks** (43.11) occupies the lowest starting rung on the ladder, his inclusion remains necessary to preserve our game caps. Investors should note the **Kyle Tucker** (75.35) matchup; while his platoon risk is marginal, his base projection remains robust enough to withstand a sub-optimal handedness split against Bratt, providing the stability our lineup requires to chase league-leading category totals.",
